## 8. NOT COVERED, AND THE STOP RULE
- **Not covered:** production, money, any human comment before "POST NOTICES", any `.env` edit, secret change, key change, `az`, **prune (even when a whole-graph rebuild fills the disk)**, any test write (no labelled create, no key, no login), **any attempt to make the database or a pooler fail to provoke a 503, a thrown-value path or a describer failure**, `POST /api/admin/migrate-tenant-data`, deploying any SHA but the pinned one, source edit, any PR or merge, force push, delete (quarantine), `docker start` of demo-service, running the `migrations` image, touching Peter's tickets or his merges, the test/doc-only tickets, preflight legs 3/4/8 and Schemathesis, the authenticated 200 paths named in CHANGED item 8.
- **STOP and mail on:** develop differing from the pin; a box REVISION other than `061c3a4f62d5`; a `.sql` in the delta; tracker moved; `.env` hash moved; a wallet hash that moved or kintsugi's on demo; infra `StartedAt` moved; a rollback; **SAME-ID on api-gateway, auth, originate, mcp-server, or on any of the other 23 swapped backends (the lock change must reach the image)**; **content (the dist fingerprint) CHANGED in any image other than api-gateway, auth, originate, mcp-server**; a non-comment content change in mcp-server; a dist difference in api-gateway, auth or originate that no source hunk of #1763, #1766, #1767, #1768 explains; a qs version other than 6.16.1 in a running swapped backend; `guardian` or `queue` UNCHANGED after the build (profile missed; fix before swapping); `FAIL-CLOSED`; disk under floor; a production host; non-final anchor row; the `migrations` image run by anything. Rolling back to a tagged image needs no answer; passing a STOP does.

