## HOLDS
- Production, money, external comms, irreversible: pause for Kam. No `az`, prune, `--no-verify`, force push, `--admin`. Never delete; quarantine. Never edit a running script (write generation beside it; before editing any script that could be mid-run, count interpreters whose `comm` is bash and whose args name it, and `lsof` it). NO git push this round (a push need is a STOP and QUESTION).
- **ADMIN CREDENTIALS (Kam).** Seat B 69th rotated `admin@secuura.com` on both boxes and added `stuart.jamieson@secuura.ai` on kintsugi. You touch no admin or user row. You do not use, print, quote or write into any artefact (notices included) the old published default for `admin@secuura.com`, anywhere. If you ever need an authenticated admin call (not planned, and the authenticated routes above are deliberately NOT exercised), read the value BY PATH from `/Volumes/DevMASTER/!CODING/Secuura/Blockchain/4_Credentials/kintsugi-admin-rotated-2026-10-27.txt` or `demo-admin-rotated-2026-10-27.txt` into a shell variable, never echo it, never put it in a file, a mail or a ticket, and ask Wednesday first.
- Exit codes on their own line, never through a pipe (`cmd > out 2>&1; rc=$?`; zsh has `$pipestatus[1]`, not `PIPESTATUS`). zsh does not word-split a scalar (inline, an array, or `bash <<'EOF'`). Never `cd` in a Bash call; absolute paths. A gating read (pin, state, restore check) is its own call, before the action it gates. Greps over text that may differ by case use `-i` with a positive control. Rotate in the 80-90 band, handover first. Never pipe an instrument's output through `head` and then measure the result. A private TMPDIR must be SHORT (tsx unix socket). Stop only the PIDs you started, never `pkill` by name.

